# Boardwright

**AI design assistant for Altium Designer.** You describe a circuit in
chat, or attach a picture or block diagram, and Boardwright builds it in
Altium: real parts checked against their datasheets, an ERC-clean
schematic, then a routed, DRC-clean board and the fab package.

Boardwright ships as a **Claude Code plugin** from a separate distribution
repository, `Aka8sh3/boardwright-plugin`. Users install it there; its
README ([plugin/PLUGIN-README.md](plugin/PLUGIN-README.md)) is the user
guide. **This repository is the source.**

## What is here

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `src/boardwright/` | the Boardwright layer: MCP server (wraps the engine, adds `boardwright_info`, `boardwright_start_bridge`, `boardwright_doctor`), self-preparation on start, the `boardwright` command |
| `skills/boardwright/` | the one skill: `SKILL.md` routes the job; `references/schematic.md` and `references/layout.md` hold the two procedures |
| `engine/` | submodule `Aka8sh3/boardwright-engine`: eda-agent with Boardwright's patch series (`docs/ENGINE.md`) |
| `plugin/` | plugin and marketplace manifests, `.mcp.json`, the user README, `Install-Boardwright.ps1` |
| `tools/` | `build_runtime.ps1` (portable Python + engine + Boardwright), `build_plugin.ps1` (the plugin folder), `constraints.txt` (pinned versions) |
| `tests/` | Boardwright's tests |
| `docs/` | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `ENGINE.md` |

## Build and release

On the build PC: Python 3.12 with pip, git, internet access.

```powershell
git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Aka8sh3/boardwright
cd boardwright
git clone https://github.com/Aka8sh3/boardwright-plugin dist\boardwright-plugin
.\tools\build_plugin.ps1 -Rebuild        # runtime + plugin into dist\boardwright-plugin
cd dist\boardwright-plugin
git add -A; git commit -m "Boardwright <version>"; git push
```

Users then get it with `/plugin marketplace update boardwright`.

To try a build locally before pushing:
`/plugin marketplace add C:\path\to\dist\boardwright-plugin`, then
`/plugin install boardwright@boardwright`.

## Tests

```powershell
$env:PYTHONPATH = "src;engine/src"; python -m pytest tests -q
```

The engine has its own suite in `engine/` (`python -m pytest -q`).

## Credits and licence

Boardwright is licensed under Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE`, `NOTICE`). Its engine,
which connects to Altium, is a modified version of
[eda-agent](https://github.com/salitronic/eda-agent) by George Saliba
(Apache-2.0, `LICENSES/eda-agent/`). The changes are listed in
`docs/ENGINE.md`. How the pieces fit: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
